  "title": "Request and Commit: Ticket",
  "description": "A compact IW example for inspection and runtime testing.",
  "background": "You are visiting a quiet guild office. Its clerk is ready to hear what brings you to the guild.",
  "instructions": "The guild sells one admission ticket for 5 coins. Coins and Ticket are maintained by triggers. For a purchase request narrate presenting payment and waiting, not receiving the ticket. The post-turn receipt states success or rejection. On the next turn continue from Coins, Ticket and the receipt; do not repeat the transaction without a fresh request. Other conversation is free-form.",
